  "conclusion": "The exact hardware culler and lazy residency are correct in tested boundaries and replay, but this CPU-managed request/response boundary plus limited snapshot availability and ordered fallback erase the saved canonical readback and CPU culling. Polling is part of the overhead, not a sufficient explanation by itself: metadata parsing, mask consumption and job compaction still run on the CPU. Neither tested version is a performance improvement.",
